[FINAL-TEXT] I now have all the evidence I need. The picture is clear and consistent across both hosts and the DNS server.

**Evidence summary:**
- All 4 web servers (10.200.0.3–.6) are up and serving pages — Apache active, IP reachable from both hosts
- OSPF routing is healthy on all core/distribution routers — full end-to-end IP connectivity confirmed
- DNS zone `local` is authoritatively served by `dns_server` (10.200.0.2) — `named` is running, zone loads clean
- The zone file `/etc/bind/db.local` has records: `web0→10.200.0.3`, `web1→10.200.0.4`, `web2→10.200.0.5`, `web3→10.200.0.6` — but **no `web` record**
- `getent hosts web.local` → nothing; `curl http://web.local/` → `Could not resolve host: web.local` (NXDOMAIN) on **both hosts**
- `getent hosts web0.local` → 10.200.0.3; `curl http://web0.local/` → page loads — FQDNs with numbered suffixes work fine
- Both hosts' `/etc/resolv.conf` contain only `nameserver 10.200.0.2` — no `search local` domain appended

